Arduino-usbserial-atmega16u2-Uno-Rev3.hex
=========================================

Arduino-usbserial, the USB to serial firmware of the Arduino Uno R3's
ATmega16U2, is a modified version of the USBtoSerial demonstration of
Dean Camera's LUFA library, built against LUFA 100807. The image comes
unchanged from Arduino's ArduinoCore-avr repository,
https://github.com/arduino/ArduinoCore-avr:

	firmwares/atmegaxxu2/arduino-usbserial/Arduino-usbserial-atmega16u2-Uno-Rev3.hex
	commit 11b9130371e8447920edb65a75706a6c951e51fc
	git blob d1404eef09b6ced4e3442064ce13bf2cd9a8ec26

Its sources, Arduino-usbserial.c and the files next to it, carry LUFA's
license, which LUFA's documentation calls the MIT license. Its notice,
as it appears in those sources:

  Copyright 2010  Dean Camera (dean [at] fourwalledcubicle [dot] com)

  Permission to use, copy, modify, distribute, and sell this
  software and its documentation for any purpose is hereby granted
  without fee, provided that the above copyright notice appear in
  all copies and that both that the copyright notice and this
  permission notice and warranty disclaimer appear in supporting
  documentation, and that the name of the author not be used in
  advertising or publicity pertaining to distribution of the
  software without specific, written prior permission.

  The author disclaim all warranties with regard to this
  software, including all implied warranties of merchantability
  and fitness.  In no event shall the author be liable for any
  special, indirect or consequential damages or any damages
  whatsoever resulting from loss of use, data or profits, whether
  in an action of contract, negligence or other tortious action,
  arising out of or in connection with the use or performance of
  this software.

The USB vendor and product IDs in the image (2341:0043) are Arduino's.
